@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="row justify-content-center">
    <div class="col-lg-9">
        <div class="card-clean p-4">
            <h3 class="fw-bold mb-1">Privacy Policy</h3>
            <p class="text-muted small mb-4">Effective Date: October 8, 2026 &middot; AcxiomCRM Enterprise Platform</p>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h5 class="fw-semibold">1. Information We Collect</h5>
                <p>AcxiomCRM collects and processes business information solely to facilitate customer relationship management, sales pipeline coordination, and administrative functions. Categories of data include:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Account Information:</strong> Name, work email address, system roles, encrypted credentials, and session authentication tokens.</li>
                    <li><strong>CRM Business Data:</strong> Customer contact details (name, corporate email, phone, business address), sales leads, opportunity valuations, pipeline stages, and follow-up activities.</li>
                    <li><strong>Audit and Telemetry Records:</strong> Timestamps of system actions, user identifiers, IP addresses associated with login attempts, data creation, modification, and deactivation events.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h5 class="fw-semibold">2. Purpose of Data Processing</h5>
                <p>Data stored in AcxiomCRM is utilized strictly for:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Authenticating authorized personnel and enforcing role-based permissions (Admin, Manager, Sales Executive).</li>
                    <li>Facilitating customer interactions, lead qualification, and opportunity progression.</li>
                    <li>Maintaining security audit trails to prevent unauthorized access and data tampering.</li>
                    <li>Generating real-time management reports and pipeline analytics.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h5 class="fw-semibold">3. Data Security and Encryption</h5>
                <p>AcxiomCRM enforces industry-standard technical safeguards: user passwords are cryptographically hashed using adaptive algorithms (PBKDF2/ASP.NET Core Identity standards), authentication cookies are protected with HTTP-only and SameSite flags, and database access is restricted via parameterized Entity Framework Core queries over TLS.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h5 class="fw-semibold">4. Audit Logging and Retention</h5>
                <p>Security and state changes generate append-only audit entries. These logs cannot be purged or modified by regular users and are maintained in compliance with corporate governance policies.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h5 class="fw-semibold">5. User Rights and Data Control</h5>
                <p>Authorized users may request correction or export of their profile data through their designated system administrator. Inactive records are archived in accordance with organizational retention schedules.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="mb-4">
                <h5 class="fw-semibold">6. Contact Information</h5>
                <p>For privacy inquiries or technical administration requests, contact the designated data protection officer:</p>
                <div class="p-3 bg-light border rounded small">
                    <strong>AcxiomCRM Administration Office</strong><br />
                    Email: <code>privacy@acxiomcrm.local</code><br />
                    Organization: [PROJECT_OWNER_ORGANIZATION_PLACEHOLDER]
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
